  "articleSummary": "The article argues that search is a diverse set of problems and that semantic/vector search should complement—not replace—exact-match, lexical, and fuzzy search in a hybrid architecture. It explains embeddings, vectors, semantic similarity, and technologies such as pgvector, Qdrant, Weaviate, Pinecone, Milvus, Elasticsearch, and other vector databases, comparing their deployment models, licensing, capabilities, and workload fit. Written as a practical, analytical guide for engineers making search-system decisions, it emphasizes choosing tools based on the problem rather than “embedding everything.” A recurring framing device contrasts deterministic lookups such as finding an email address with relevance-based queries such as finding articles about debugging.",
